## Abstract

Clickbait is best understood not as â€œbad headlines,â€ but as a **packaging technology for attention**. It converts uncertainty, emotion, identity, and platform visibility into clicks, views, comments, shares, ad impressions, affiliate conversions, or ranking signals. Its defining problem is **warrant failure**: the headline, thumbnail, preview card, or prompt makes a promise that the destination content does not adequately justify. Clickbait can appear in professional newsrooms, content farms, MFA sites, YouTube thumbnails, TikTok captions, Google Discover cards, affiliate â€œbest-of
